Subject: [PATCH] ARM64EC: poll the suspend doorbell before conditional backward branches

The JIT polls the suspend doorbell (EmitSuspendInterruptCheck: load the doorbell word, cbz, brk #0xCAFE)
at block entry and before a pending UNCONDITIONAL backward branch. CondJump emits its b.cond / cbz /
cbnz / tbz / tbnz straight to the target, so a loop whose back-edge is the taken side of a conditional
branch — the canonical spin-wait `pause; test; je 1b` — never observes a pending suspend while it spins;
with multiblock compilation such a loop lives in one compiled unit, so no block-entry poll is reached
either. Under the ARM64EC suspend contract (wine, like Windows, does not stop a thread in simulation: it
rings the doorbell and GetThreadContext waits for the poll) a runtime that stops the world with
SuspendThread + GetThreadContext therefore hangs whenever the target spins waiting on a thread that is
already suspended.

Poll before the conditional branch when its target is already emitted (a backward edge). The check is
flag-neutral and uses a scratch register, so it is safe in front of a branch that consumes NZCV, and it
sits at a guest instruction boundary: a trap there reconstructs the state at the branch and the branch
re-executes on resume. Cost: one L1 load and one never-taken branch per loop iteration, the poll every
safepoint-based managed runtime places on loop back-edges. Test and measurements: propnix
emulators/wine-mono/tests/spin.c and docs/research/mono-arm64ec.md.
--- a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/JIT/BranchOps.cpp
+++ b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/JIT/BranchOps.cpp
@@ -244,6 +244,14 @@
 
   auto TrueTargetLabel = JumpTarget(Op->TrueBlock);
 
+  // A conditional branch to an already-emitted block is a loop back-edge: poll the suspend doorbell before
+  // it, as the block loop does before unconditional backward branches, so a loop closed by a conditional
+  // branch can be suspended. The check is flag-neutral and sits at a guest instruction boundary; the branch
+  // re-executes on resume.
+  if (TrueTargetLabel->Backward.Location) {
+    EmitSuspendInterruptCheck();
+  }
+
   if (Op->FromNZCV) {
     b_OrRestart(MapCC(Op->Cond), TrueTargetLabel);
   } else {
